###
### DATABASE SETUP REQUIRED
###
### The database is currently empty. Run the seed script first:
### PGPASSWORD=password psql -U user -d moviedb -h localhost -f scripts/seeddb.sql
### 
### This will load 1000 movies with directors and genres from TMDB data.
### After seeding, the list and filter requests below will return data.
###

### Movie Rating Backend API - REST Client
### Base URL Configuration
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
@apiVersion = /api/v1

### Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Accept: application/json

###
### MOVIES ENDPOINTS - RETRIEVE (after seeding)
###

### List Movies - Paginated (Default)
GET {{baseUrl}}{{apiVersion}}/movies?page=1&page_size=10
Accept: application/json

### List Movies - Next Page
GET {{baseUrl}}{{apiVersion}}/movies?page=2&page_size=10
Accept: application/json

### List Movies - Filter by Title
GET {{baseUrl}}{{apiVersion}}/movies?page=1&page_size=10&title=Avatar
Accept: application/json

### List Movies - Filter by Release Year
GET {{baseUrl}}{{apiVersion}}/movies?page=1&page_size=10&release_year=2009
Accept: application/json

### List Movies - Filter by Genre
GET {{baseUrl}}{{apiVersion}}/movies?page=1&page_size=10&genre=Action
Accept: application/json

### Get Movie by ID (will work after seeding)
GET {{baseUrl}}{{apiVersion}}/movies/100
Accept: application/json

### Get Movie by ID (try another)
GET {{baseUrl}}{{apiVersion}}/movies/500
Accept: application/json

###
### MOVIES ENDPOINTS - CREATE/UPDATE/DELETE
###
### NOTE: These require valid director_id and genre_ids from the database.
### After running the seed script, use valid IDs from:
### - PGPASSWORD=password psql -U user -d moviedb -h localhost
### - SELECT id FROM directors LIMIT 1;
### - SELECT id FROM genres LIMIT 2;
###

### Create Movie (AFTER seeding - use real director and genre IDs)
POST {{baseUrl}}{{apiVersion}}/movies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Test Movie 2026",
  "release_year": 2026,
  "cast": "Test Actor 1, Test Actor 2",
  "description": "A test movie created for API validation",
  "director_id": 2,
  "genre_ids": [1, 2]
}

### Update Movie
PUT {{baseUrl}}{{apiVersion}}/movies/100
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Updated Test Movie",
  "description": "Updated description for testing",
  "cast": "Updated Actor 1, Updated Actor 2"
}

### Delete Movie (use with caution!)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}{{apiVersion}}/movies/9999

###
### RATINGS ENDPOINTS
###

### Rate a Movie (1-10 scale)
POST {{baseUrl}}{{apiVersion}}/movies/100/ratings?score=9
Accept: application/json

### Get All Ratings for a Movie
GET {{baseUrl}}{{apiVersion}}/movies/100/ratings
Accept: application/json

###
### NOTES
###
# - Make sure the server is running on localhost:8000
# - Use the VS Code REST Client extension to run these requests
# 
# DATABASE SETUP REQUIRED:
# - The database is currently EMPTY (no directors or genres)
# - Run the seed script to populate with 1000 movies:
#   PGPASSWORD=password psql -U user -d moviedb -h localhost -f scripts/seeddb.sql
# - After seeding, all requests will work with real data
#
# REQUIRED FIELDS for MovieCreate: title, release_year, director_id, genre_ids
# OPTIONAL FIELDS: cast, description
# ALL RESPONSES follow the format: {"status": "success", "data": {...}}
